ten per-app EXECUTE blocks directly in isolated worktrees; the start-orchestration bootstrap remains suspended until the repos are in known state. Claude still provides independent A5 review/approval before merge/deploy. Full handoff + recon + open decisions: [[2026-06-01 1815 — Four-app v1 plan + Codex execution handoff]]. Detailed per-app checklist: [[MOC - v1 Verification Steps]]. Cross-app context source: [[Four-app v1 control ledger]].\n\n**Autonomous = additive / reversible / observable** (STRATEGY\'s guardrail). A gate = destructive, irreversible, external-facing, or a judgment call.\n\n**Browser V1 acceptance gate:** fixture seeding, SQL assertions, unit/integration tests, GitHub Actions, and Playwright automation are scaffolding/supporting evidence only. Browser V1 is not accepted until Chrome/Chrome DevTools real-browser execution proves the persona flows through visible UI outcomes, screenshots, console/network inspection where relevant, and browser-console probes where required. Do not use Codex in-app browser / MAP / `iab` as the acceptance surface unless Jarrad explicitly reverses this.\n\n**Browser V1 UI-created data rule:** data setup is part of the browser test. For [[Closer Lab]] and [[BMH Institute]], create fixture/content/test records through Chrome/DevTools browser UI wherever the app UI supports creation or editing. Direct database/API writes are exception-only supporting setup for things the UI cannot create, such as auth bootstrap when no signup/admin UI exists, and must be labeled as non-acceptance evidence.\n\n**2026-06-02 browser-surface correction:** Jarrad first reset [[Closer Lab]] and [[BMH Institute]] Browser V1 acceptance to zero, then superseded the MAP/in-app-browser requirement with Chrome/DevTools real-browser execution. Current controller evidence shows [[BMH Institute]] residual proof closed and [[Closer Lab]] Browser V1 markers closed for pre-read persistence, signed embed-token proof, and scoring/runtime. [[Sandra]] production-readiness proof is GO as of 2026-06-11. The 2026-06-18 active-front reset (skip-trace/CASS preflight, filter preset discoverability, bulk tag creation, Sendillo-era Overview KPI visibility) is now CLEARED 2026-06-19 — all four shipped via merged PRs #288–#300, plus Messages disposition/outcomes hardening (#298/#299/#300). Remaining [[Sandra]] threads: PR #287 (hide dead-dispositioned leads from the kanban — OPEN, awaiting NULL-handling review) and the bulk-SMS→Campaigns KPI tracking gap (June 19 run, job `72b0e08d`, 7,547 messages queued with `campaignId=null`) — forward fix now in **PR #301 (OPEN, awaiting review)** which requires a campaign name + auto-creates + stamps `campaign_id`, with the 2026-06-19 architect P1s folded in; the **June 19 backfill is still pending** (designed, not applied — must match by `property_id` intersection, not the created_at window which over-captures by 6).\n\n**2026-06-02 trust reset:** Jarrad challenged the controller\'s Playwright-heavy verification and does not trust acceptance unless it is revalidated in Chrome/DevTools. Treat Playwright/CI/API/DB evidence as support only. Fresh revalidation so far: [[BMH Institute]] Chrome snapshot/screenshot `/tmp/browser-revalidation-bmh-institute-current.*` visibly shows `Lesson complete`, with separate Sandra outcome confirmation `/tmp/browser-revalidation-bmh-institute-outcome.json`; [[Closer Lab]] member Chrome snapshot/screenshot `/tmp/browser-revalidation-closer-member-recording.*` visibly shows recording `72ad25d8-1b09-4ef9-\n\n### CURATED: Home.md\n# Home — BMH OS\n\nThe control room. Start every session here.\n\n## North star\n[[STRATEGY]] — the one goal and the current bottleneck.\n\n## The v1 push\n[[MOC - v1]] — every app\'s checklist to version 1.\n\n## The three layers — where things live (read this if unsure)\nThe vault separates the *goal*, the *scoreboard*, and *today\'s work* into three files. They change at very different rates — don\'t confuse them:\n\n| File | Role | Changes |\n|------|------|---------|\n| [[STRATEGY]] | the **one goal + why** (north star) | almost never — only on milestone-done or a real pivot |\n| [[MOC - v1]] | the **scoreboard** — what "done" concretely means, as checkboxes | when a box gets ticked |\n| [[_Active]] | **what I\'m doing right now / next step** | every session |\n\nRule of thumb: each layer is a *map* of the one below it. STRATEGY → MOC (definition of done) → _Active (current step) → linked detail notes. A MOC is a **map, not a document** — it stays scannable and links *down* to detailed notes rather than holding the detail inline. If you\'re rewriting STRATEGY often, that churn probably belongs in _Active.\n\nPromotion: AI writes raw captures to `_inbox/`; **you** promote what matters into `projects/ decisions/ contracts/ sources/` (good friction). Nothing in those folders changes without your OK.\n\n## Apps\n- [[Sandra]] · CRM\n- [[Closer Lab]] · call practice\n- [[BMH Institute]] · LMS\n- [[Jitter]] · dialer\n\n## Content\n- [[BMH Training Course]] · 19-module onboarding course (feeds [[BMH Institute]])\n\n## How this vault works\n[[conventions]] — the rules the AI follows when writing here.\nRaw AI captures land in `_inbox/`; you promote what matters (good friction).\n\n## Tooling\n[[skills]] — index of custom Claude Code skills (e.g. custom-codex-watcher) and how to invoke them.\n\n## Map — entry points\n- [[STRATEGY]] — the one goal + current bottleneck.\n- [[MOC - v1]] — every app\'s checklist to v1.\n- [[MOC - v1 Verification Steps]] — detailed per-app happy-path steps behind the MOC boxes.\n- [[_Active|Active priorities]] — what now.\n- [[_Active-Pairs|Active pairs]] — live Claude↔Codex orchestration registry.\n- Apps: [[Sandra]] · [[Closer Lab]] · [[BMH Institute]] · [[Jitter]].\n- [[skills]] — custom Claude Code skills index.\n- [[claude-codex-loop]] — autonomous execution loop.\n\n## Map — folders\n- `projects/` — promoted app & project notes.\n- `decisions/` — ADR-style decision records.\n- `contracts/` — agreed data shape two+ apps depend on (e.g. `call.completed`), written once so neither side drifts.\n- `sources/` — reference / extracted source material.\n- `mocs/` — Maps of Content.\n- `_inbox/` — AI write zone (raw per-session captures).\n- `_meta/` — conventions, tags, credentials, skills, capture daemon, briefing.\n- `_ai-context/` — AI-integration & orchestration docs.\n\n### CURATED: projects/BMH Institute.md\n---\ntype: project\nstatus: active\ntags: [lms, institute]\ncreated: 2026-05-30\nupdated: 2026-06-02\nrelated: ["[[MOC - v1]]", "[[Sandra]]", "[[Closer Lab]]", "[[Four-app v1 control ledger]]", "[[2026-06-01 2233 — BMH Institute Browser V1 testing prompt]]"]\n---\n# BMH Institute\n\nTraining LMS for VAs. Next.js 16 + Supabase. **Live** at institute.bmhgroupkc.com (v1.1 shipped 2026-05-09).\n\n## v1 happy path\nInvite VA → set password → work assigned program → complete course → certificate.\n\n## Browser V1 fixture\n- Persistent browser testing prompt: [[2026-06-01 2233 — BMH Institute Browser V1 testing prompt]]\n- Control context: [[Four-app v1 control ledger]]\n- Acceptance surface is Chrome/Chrome DevTools real-browser execution with visible UI outcomes. Playwright/backend checks are supporting evidence only.\n- Browser V1 data creation must happen through the browser UI wherever the UI supports it. Create programs, courses, modules, lessons, content, quizzes, assignments, invites, submissions, and certificate-triggering flows through UI clicks instead of direct database population when possible.\n- Direct database/API writes are exception-only supporting setup for things the UI cannot create, such as auth/persona bootstrap if no UI path exists. Existing database-seeded Browser V1 data may remain for Jarrad but does not count as acceptance unless equivalent UI-created flows are proven.\n- 2026-06-02 correction: acceptance surface superseded from in-app/MAP browser to Chrome/DevTools real-browser execution; controller residual