llback tag recorded, lane closed. (source: [[2026-06-01 2121 — BMH Institute PR #79 merged, post-merge gates gr (019e860c)]])\n- 2026-06-01 — PR #79 merged (head a737fac); E2E write-path rerun pending with explicit env mapping; branch drift and stale process blockers noted. (source: [[2026-06-01 2138 — Institute v1 executor respawn, PR#79 merged (019e862a)]])\n- 2026-06-02 — Handoff prompt to create persistent BMH Institute Browser V1 user-emulation fixture lab, including role group\n\n### CURATED: projects/BMH Training Course.md\n---\ntype: project\nstatus: active\ntags: [training, course]\ncreated: 2026-06-04\nupdated: 2026-07-02\nrelated: ["[[BMH Institute]]", "[[Sandra]]", "[[STRATEGY]]", "[[Home]]"]\n---\n# BMH Training Course\n\nThe **BMH Follow-Up Specialist** onboarding course — 19 modules of video + transcript + quiz content. A **content-production** workstream (not code), feeding the [[BMH Institute]] LMS that delivers it. Avatar is **Andrea** (HeyGen UI label; called **Sandra** in older scripts — same avatar), voice **Hope**.\n\n## Where it lives\n- **Content (in-vault):** `BMH Training Course/` at the vault root — 436 MB. Markdown/json/txt are git-tracked; heavy binaries (PDF/xlsx/mp3/srt) live in the folder for Obsidian but are **gitignored** to keep the repo lean.\n- **Canonical README inside the content:** `BMH Training Course/README.md`\n- **Original fallback (untouched):** `$HOME/MyBrain/Projects/BMH Group Training/` — copied additively 2026-06-04, not moved.\n- **Video production (2026-07-02):** lives in the **BMH Institute repo**, not the vault. Planning (git-tracked) in `Sites/BMH apps/BMH Institute/docs/course-production/` (visual-bible + shotlists); style refs + cast/object boards in `docs/design/`; generated PNGs/MP4s in `course-assets/` (gitignored, regenerable). On branch `claude/course-production` (commit d66675b). Style = flat sticker system; images generated via **Codex `gpt-image-2`** against the design-folder refs. Transcripts/quizzes stay canonical in the vault.\n\n## Where we left off — Phase 1: Lock Content (verified from git, Apr 30 2026)\nSlot-by-slot review of `Thinkific/_master-transcripts.md` (193 KB) for opening/ending flow, continuity, and **transitions**. Per-slot decisions live in `Thinkific/transcripts/changes/SLOT-NN*.md`.\n\n| Slot | Module | Review status |\n|------|--------|---------------|\n| 1 | Welcome & Mindset | ✅ locked (4 decisions) |\n| 2 | Terms Glossary | ✅ locked (6 decisions) |\n| 3 | Tech Stack & Systems | ✅ locked (7 decisions) |\n| 4 | Humanizing the Lead | ✅ locked (6 decisions) — **last action, Apr 30 20:31** |\n| 5 | The BMH Offer Model | ✅ locked (2026-07-01) — 5a + 5b decision files |\n| 6–19 | Sales Pipeline → Career Growth | ✅ locked (2026-07-01) — fleet pre-review + fixes applied directly to master |\n\n**Phase 1 (Lock Content) COMPLETE 2026-07-01.** All 19 slots reviewed; fixes applied to `_master-transcripts.md` (backups: `_master-transcripts.backup-2026-07-01.md`, `.backup-prerebrand-2026-07-01.md`).\n\n> **Phase 1.5 (Jarrad line-by-line pass) COMPLETE 2026-07-01 (evening).** Jarrad read every module transcript 1→19 in-session and approved each. Additional changes: Asana removed course-wide (tasks → Sandra); "the BMH Group" prefix normalized; instructor renamed Andrea everywhere (incl. Welcome intro); cold-vs-warm objection framing scene added to Module 9; Welcome got a plain "what we do" scene; Module 13 opener rewritten; Module 14 got an opener + dedupe (44 scenes); sign-off variety pass (no more repeated "see you in the next lesson"); dozens of quote/punctuation normalizations; Module 17 comp numbers confirmed current; Module 18 lesson-1 capstone outro fixed. **The master transcript is RECORD-READY.**\n\n> **2026-07-01 — Phase 1 complete.** Fleet pre-review (staging: `Thinkific/transcripts/changes/_review-staging/`) + live decision session with Jarrad. Applied to the master transcript: all 326 voice-direction tags stripped (emotion directed per-scene in HeyGen instead); rebrand REsimpli→Sandra (29), Thinkific→BMH Institute, Jarrad→"your manager"; instructor renamed to **Andrea** (5 spots — "Sandra" now only ever means the CRM); "the BMH Group" prefix normalized (31); all outro/bridge fixes (Slots 9, 10 bookends, 13, 15, 16, 17, 18×2, 19 finale close); Slot 8 callback genericized. PropStream/HubStaff/DialPad confirmed still in the stack; county channel list confirmed current. **Videos NOT yet recorded — Jarrad records fresh from this locked master.**\n>\n> **Still open before recording:** segment the 3\n\n### CURATED: projects/Closer Lab.md\n---\ntype: project\nstatus: active\ntags: [practice, closer-lab]\ncreated: 2026-05-30\nupdated: 2026-06-02\nrelated: ["[[MOC - v1]]", "[[Sandra]]", "[[BMH Institute]]", "[[Four-app v1 control ledger]]", "[[2026-06-02 — Closer Lab Browser V1 exhaustive testing prompt]]"]\n---\n# Closer Lab\n\nAI roleplay / call-practice. Next.js + Supabase, **live on Railway** (persistent WebSocket relay).\nEmbeds into [[BMH Institute]] via JWT iframe.\n\n- **Live URL (production, canonical):** https://web-production-a302.up.railway.app\n- Repo: `biginkc/closer-lab` · local: `$HOME/Sites/BMH apps/Closer Lab`\n- ⚠️ `closerlab.bmhgroup.com` (in `_archive/bmh-platform-monorepo-attempt/`) is a **dead/aspirational** domain from an abandoned monorepo — not live. Do not use.\n\n## v1 happy path\nLog in → run a roleplay scenario → get a score against the BMH playbook.\n\n## Browser V1 testing lab\n- Persistent browser testing prompt: [[2026-06-02 — Closer Lab Browser V1 exhaustive testing prompt]]\n- Control context: [[Four-app v1 control ledger]]\n- Acceptance surface is Chrome/Chrome DevTools real-browser execution with visible UI outcomes. GitHub Actions, Playwright, SQL, unit/integration/build checks, and fixture workflows are scaffolding only.\n- Browser V1 data creation must happen through the browser UI wherever the UI supports it. Create labs, roleplay attempts, scoring/rubric artifacts, share flows, and embed proofs through UI clicks instead of direct database population when possible.\n- Direct database/API writes are exception-only supporting setup for things the UI cannot create, such as auth bootstrap if no UI path exists. Existing database-seeded Browser V1 data may remain for Jarrad but does not count as acceptance unless equivalent UI-created flows are proven.\n- 2026-06-02 correction: acceptance surface superseded from in-app/MAP browser to Chrome/DevTools real-browser execution; production Browser V1 markers are closed for pre-read persistence, BMH Institute signed embed-token path, and scoring/runtime.\n- 2026-06-02T07:14Z controller update: current acceptance surface is Chrome/DevTools real-browser evidence per Jarrad\'s later correction. Production owner/member UI-created Browser V1 data is in progress for `BROWSER-V1 CHROME Role Play 202606020640`. The Pre-read persistence marker is closed: admin Pre-read editor was corrected through the visible Chrome tab, saved with 142 chars and rendered preview, and member refresh showed the briefing plus `Start when ready`. Evidence: `/tmp/closer-browser-v1-chrome/23-owner-preread-clean-visible-before-save.txt`, `/tmp/closer-browser-v1-chrome/24-owner-preread-clean-saved.png`, `/tmp/closer-browser-v1-chrome/25-member-preread-visible-after-clean-save.png`, `/tmp/closer-browser-v1-chrome/25-member-preread-visible-after-clean-save.txt`. Remaining Browser V1 markers are signed embed-token proof and scoring proof with real learner speech or safe fixture transcript.\n- 2026-06-02T07:23Z controller update: signed embed-token proof is closed through the live [[BMH Institute]] production lesson path. The repo walkthrough lesson constant was stale and returned 404, but live learner navigation found `Embedded Practice Preview` at `/lessons/4d24fa5d-7191-4e50-ab3a-fdc456112c14`; BMH Institute minted the Closer iframe, Closer rendered `Closer Lab Demo: Skeptical Seller` with `Start when ready`, and clicking it enter